course: dictionary
lesson: 4905
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word image is a good example. «You're the very image of her» does not mean a photo. It means someone looks just like another person.
explain: Read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits. «Photos get edited, and AI can make images with small mistakes like extra fingers.» Here images are pictures made by a camera, a drawing or a computer. Then try your meaning in the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Image can also mean a reflection, the picture you see in a mirror or in water. A mirror image is the picture you see when you look in a mirror. The words around the word, like mirror or water, show you which meaning to use.
fact: Image means a picture, photo or drawing, on paper or on a screen.
fact: Image can also mean a picture of something in your mind, or a reflection in a mirror, lens or water.
fact: Image can mean the way other people see someone or something.
fact: In «the very image of her», image means looks just like her.
fact: Pictures can be edited or made by AI, so they can be fake or have small mistakes.
exercise: «You're the very image of her.» What does image mean here? | A reflection in a mirror | A picture in a book | *Looks just like | A photo on a screen
exercise: «Photos get edited, and AI can make images with small mistakes like extra fingers.» What are images in this sentence? | *Pictures made by a camera, a drawing or a computer | Hooks that fasten a dress | Sounds from a phone | Mirrors that show you your face
exercise: Ella closes her eyes and sees an image of the beach in her mind. What does image mean? | A reflection in a pond | The way people see her at school | A photo that has been edited | *A picture of something in your mind
test: Jade looks in the mirror and sees her image. What is her image? | A fast run | A painting of a tree | A loud sound | *The reflection of herself
test: Sam wants a good image at school, so he is always kind. What does image mean here? | A mirror on the wall | *The way other people see him | A drawing of a dog | A photo of his school
exam: A mirror makes an image that is reversed left to right. Which meaning of image fits best? | *A reflection, the picture you see in a mirror | A photo you can print out | A song you can sing | The way people think of you
